nebflow.agent.FreezeSilenceSpec:
  + provider failure freeze: ZERO upward notification (parent mailbox + parent ref), panel says needs-you-but-auto-recoverable, wake entry stays 0.485s
  + one wave of 6 provider-failure freezes: notification count = 0 and the quiet digest reads 6 1.787s
  + deterministic-defect freezes produce exactly ONE aggregated alert for the whole wave (and no repeat on the next tick) 1.041s
  + auto-resume: waits while no provider serves, then resumes the SAME session via UserInput (never RestartAgent) with zero notification 0.489s
  + auto-resume budget: capped attempts with growing gaps, and only an exhausted budget escalates to ONE alert 0.495s
  + auto-resume backoff: exponential with a CAP, and the retry schedule is never a fixed short loop 0.016s
  + escalation horizon (重写, fallback 废除批): a provider freeze stays silent inside AND past the 30-minute horizon — provider digest leg retired (zero upward notify) 0.506s
  + provider-fault table: every recoverable family is silent, every deterministic defect still notifies 0.008s
  + fallback chain: a Down model elsewhere never blocks the resume (there IS a usable model in the queue) 0.5s
  + real failures still notify: a deterministic defect freezes AND reaches the author as one alert 0.491s
  + flow-notify: an infrastructure-fault node failure is never reported upward, a deterministic one still is 0.012s
