nebflow.agent.DelegateRevivalSpec:
  + V1: eligible orphan revives from transcript checkpoint; the continued turn WITHOUT a declaration is REMINDED (matrix complete×idle), never auto-completed to the parent 1.129s
  + V2(重写): revival budget exhausted → salvage chain (failed, zero notify), zero spawn 0.213s
  + V3: missing seat directory → not revived (skip reason recorded), salvaged 0.217s
  + V4: kill-switch off → all orphans salvaged, zero revival 0.216s
  + V5: revival chain across successive crashes — revive, re-revive, then budget-exhausted salvage 2.635s
  + V6: subtask-source orphan is never revived (existing salvage semantics unchanged) 0.231s
  + V7: external-executor record is never revived (Mail continuation is the runtime leg) 0.216s
  + V8: author's fake-interrupt scenario — salvaged row flagged interrupted folds once the ledger adjudicates completed 0.224s
  + V10: PURE standby (zero in-flight evidence) at engine restart → still refused, salvage settles failed — 案A semantics preserved 0.234s
  + V11: standby WHILE its own chain is still in flight (non-terminal scope node) → auto-revived (BB1 form, author ruling 2026-11-04 11:27) 0.23s
  + V12: standby + DIRTY worktree (uncommitted work in the seat) → auto-revived 0.305s
  + V13: standby + branch ahead of its base (unmerged deliverable commits) → auto-revived 0.336s
  + V14: cancel tombstone WINS over in-flight evidence — a cancelled delegate is never revived (author: only manual cancel/close stay dead) 0.204s
  + V15: failed row carrying the restart-loss fingerprint → revivable on the next boot (no manual Mail needed) 0.206s
  + V16: failed row from a NATURAL failure (no restart fingerprint) → never picked up by the revival leg 0.203s
  + V17: failed row with the fingerprint but an EXHAUSTED budget → no revival (bounded, no infinite loop) 0.204s
  + V9: cancel tombstone on record → sweep refuses revival, salvage settles failed (R1 三路径·boot sweep 腿) 0.198s
