nebflow.gateway.NfTicketRoutesSpec:
  + A1: a request without a ticket is 401 (ticket-only read leg, R5) 0.007s
  + A2: a ticket bound to another path is 403 path-mismatch 0.004s
  + A3: an expired ticket is 403 expired 1.314s
  + A4: R4 = unlimited inside the TTL — five reads on one ticket all 200 0.011s
  + A5/A6: credential paths are 403 even WITH a valid ticket (identity pattern + R2 inode) 0.006s
  + A7: a file outside the protected namespaces still serves (no over-blocking) 0.007s
  + A8: the extension gate is RETIRED — a non-whitelisted, credential-clean file serves (2026-10-07 flip) 0.005s
  + A9: a symlink into a credential file is refused (realpath normalization, C1-1/C1-2) 0.005s
  + A10: a hard link to a credential file is refused ((dev,ino) guard, R2) 0.008s
  + A11/A16: the issuer rejects credential paths and never signs them; non-credential paths all sign 0.01s
  + issuer: requires the gateway token (403 without it) 0.005s
  + A15: GET /api/nf-authcheck is 204 with a valid credential, 403 otherwise, never touches disk 0.005s
  + A15-slide: a session-rail authcheck re-emits the cookie with a fresh Max-Age; Bearer hits emit nothing 0.01s
  + A17: `<dataRoot>/docs/**` mints a ticket and reads 200 (author ruling #687-A, existing chain only) 0.008s
  + A17-counter (2026-10-07 flip): former namespace refusals serve; ONLY credential identity/inode stay refused 0.007s
  + policy: P1 is PathUtil.dataRoot (never a hardcoded home directory) 0.001s
  + policy: a newly added data-root directory SERVES after the 2026-10-07 flip (namespace default-deny retired) 0.004s
  + policy: P3 namespace is RETIRED (2026-10-07 flip) — repo files, project .nebflow and evidence alike serve; credentials still refuse 0.002s
  + policy: production P3 root is <cwd>/.nebflow (R1), not the workspace root 0.0s
nebflow.gateway.TextStreamSpec:
  + threshold: ≤8MiB stays direct, >8MiB streams, binary never streams 0.001s
  + pit ① — the streaming descriptor always carries a non-empty itemType 0.0s
  + index: anchors land on every stride-th line start and totalLines is exact 0.003s
  + index: a trailing newline does not open a phantom line, anchors past EOF are dropped 0.0s
  + index: streaming the same body in chunks equals building it whole 0.001s
  + index: empty body has zero lines and a usable anchor 0.0s
  + index: anchorFor is the largest anchor ≤ the offset; anchorForLine is the jump primitive 0.0s
  + window: text decodes, lineCount counts whole and partial lines, eof tracks the file end 0.002s
  + window: invalid UTF-8 and a split multi-byte character decode with replacement, never throw 0.0s
  + firstLine refinement is anchor line + newlines in the residual span 0.0s
  + index cache: hit refreshes recency, miss is a no-op, eviction drops the LRU entry 0.002s
