nebflow.gateway.ConsoleTakeoverSpec:
  + A1 second fresh session takes over: owner flips, old owner's live conns get takeover frame 0.006s
  + A2 same-session reconnect (refresh) silently resumes: no frame, owner unchanged 0.0s
  + A3 owner drop never yields: disconnect keeps ownership, resume is silent 0.001s
  + A3b a session's disconnect must not wipe other sessions' conn ledger (reverse-kick targets survive) 0.001s
  + A4 retake flips ownership back and reverse-kicks the new owner 0.002s
  + A5 past-owner reconnect does NOT auto-reclaim: it lands superseded, owner untouched 0.001s
  + A6 zombie recycle (disconnect of every conn) emits zero frames and keeps ownership 0.001s
  + A4b http-leg retakeBySession flips ownership and reverse-kicks (same core as ws leg) 0.002s
  + A4c http-leg retake lands even with NO live conn for the retaking session 0.0s
  + A4d http-leg retake when already owner is idempotent Ok(0) with zero frames 0.001s
  + A7 master switch off: registry is a full no-op (no claims, no frames) 0.001s
  + A8 unregistered conn (bearer rail bypass) retake is refused; frame shapes pinned 0.001s
  + A9 fresh claim wins even when the incumbent has no live conn (best-effort push) 0.0s
  + A10 takeover pushes reach every live conn of the displaced session 0.001s
  + B1 content gate: superseded session stops receiving data frames; takeover protocol still passes 0.002s
  + B2 content gate: owner session passes every frame 0.001s
  + B3 content gate: master switch off is identity (zero drift) 0.0s
  + B4 content gate: owner-unset connect window passes bootstrap frames 0.0s
  + B5 real WsHub wiring: broadcast stops feeding superseded conns; retake reopens the gate 0.003s
  + A11 single instance never sees a takeover frame (no self-conflict) 0.0s
  + A12 silent reseat (same clientId, NEW session id) resumes silently — the false-positive root 0.0s
  + A13 background resume / refresh: same clientId reconnect with stale conn alive stays silent 0.001s
  + A14 genuine takeover: two distinct clientIds ⇒ takeover frame to the OLD client only 0.001s
  + A15 undecidable identity (either side without clientId) never prompts and never kicks 0.001s
  + A16 stale instance is swept on next connect: owner cleared, zero takeover frame 0.001s
  + A17 content gate follows identity: proven-different gated, unprovable passes 0.002s
