nebflow.gateway.ConsoleTakeoverIdentifySpec:
  + S1 phone declares identity in-band after a query-less handshake ⇒ desktop is kicked with a takeover frame 0.009s
  + S2 silent reseat via in-band declaration (same clientId, NEW session id) stays silent 0.001s
  + S3 in-band declaration is a no-op when the handshake already carried the same clientId 0.001s
  + S4 two tabs of one browser declaring the same identity merge into one instance account, zero frames 0.001s
  + S5 after migration the displaced instance's every live conn receives the takeover frame 0.001s
  + S6 missing or malformed identity declarations are inert 0.002s
  + S7 master switch off: in-band declaration is a full no-op 0.001s
  + S8 past-owner reconnect that declares identity lands superseded, never auto-reclaims 0.001s
  + S9 content gate follows the declared identity (superseded instance stops receiving data frames) 0.003s
  + S10 http-leg retake keyed by the declared identity flips ownership without self-conflict 0.001s
